    tldr: "A general hospital in central Tokyo, run by the mutual aid federation for national civil servants, that is a government-designated regional hospital for cancer care and treats cancer alongside other illnesses a patient may have.",
    summary: "Toranomon Hospital, in Toranomon, Minato, Tokyo, is run by the Federation of National Public Service Personnel Mutual Aid Associations (国家公務員共済組合連合会). Its cancer care page says it is a regional cancer care cooperation base hospital (地域がん診療連携拠点病院), providing training for cancer staff, consultation support for patients and families and cancer information, and that it works in cancer genomic medicine. The hospital describes itself as a general hospital offering cancer care comparable to a specialist cancer hospital, with internal medicine specialists who allow treatment of patients with heart, lung or other coexisting disease, a geriatric medicine department for older patients, endoscopic surgery and robot-assisted surgery (introduced in July 2019), a clinical oncology department for anticancer drug treatment and a radiation oncology department, round-the-clock emergency care for patients under cancer treatment, a palliative care team, a cancer consultation support centre and second opinions. Newsweek and Statista's World's Best Specialized Hospitals 2026 list for oncology ranks it 278.",
